  "id": "nmr",
  "term": "NMR",
  "definition": "NMR refers to nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy, an analytical method used in metabolomics to monitor changes in metabolite levels. Compared with mass spectrometry methods, it is less sensitive but more reproducible, non-destructive, needs little sample preparation, and provides quantitative and structural information that helps identify metabolites.",
